Release 3.7.0.

Changelog: 02-11-2026 00:48:53

Release 3.6.0.

Changelog: 02-11-2026 00:23:01

Added. A warning when the device runs hot during a game (core's heat.py; owner, 02-11-2026): when the CPU or the GPU stays above 90 °C for half a minute, a banner shows at the top of the screen over RPCS3 and the controller rumbles three times, again at most every five minutes; the game goes on. When the game ends, the log says how hot the chip got and for how long. The wiki says so.

Changelog: 01-11-2026 23:28:28

Added. A game in Steam renamed or moved keeps its mark when the app can tell it is the same game (its title ID or serial, or a disc image's size): LT Refresh, or the next start, shows it under its new name with the mark, and Update Steam puts it in Steam under that name and takes the old shortcut out (core's renamed.py). Its shortcut no longer starts the emulator with a file that is not there: it shows a screen that says the game is no longer there and what to do (core's gone screen; owner, 01-11-2026). The pane's information and the wiki say so.

Changelog: 01-11-2026 22:54:19

Added. LT Refresh on Your games reads the game folders again: a game put there, renamed or taken away while the app is open shows at once, and the status line says when Steam no longer matches the marks (a game in Steam renamed: its shortcut started the emulator with a file no longer there; mark it again, then Update Steam takes the old shortcut out). Before, the list was read only when the app started (owner, 01-11-2026). The pane's information and the wiki say so.

Changelog: 01-11-2026 21:51:43

Release 3.5.1.

Changelog: 01-11-2026 18:11:39

Release 3.5.0.

Changelog: 01-11-2026 16:37:12

Added. The app's own game folder (owner, 30-10-2026: fixed folders, no folder selecting): Games\PS3 in the user's
folder, made when the app opens with Games\PS3\Firmware in it, and Games\PS3 on each SD card or USB drive that has
one; Your games looks there, in RPCS3's dev_hdd0 and in the disc games RPCS3 knows (library.fixed()). The PS3's
firmware put in Games\PS3\Firmware is given to RPCS3 by itself (owner, 01-11-2026: firmware taken in automatically)
when the app opens, when the RPCS3 card gets the focus and after RPCS3 is installed, while RPCS3 is closed: a file
whose version (read from the PUP, its file 0x100) is installed already is left alone, and so is the file given to
RPCS3 last as it is (its name, size and time in the app's settings), so a file RPCS3 refused is not given again until
it changes (userdata.pup_version(), library.firmware_file()). The file stays. A package (.pkg) or a license (.rap,
.edat) put in the game folders is a short row of Your games, "PKG", "PKG update" or "License"; A installs that one,
X Install all every one, the licenses first and the updates last, each in a run of RPCS3 without its window; a
license is a row only while RPCS3 does not keep it (userdata.waiting()). Nothing is deleted before the user decides
what to keep (owner, 01-11-2026: before deleting anything, let the user decide what to keep; core's keep.py): a page
lists what would go, a row each with its size, every row marked Delete at first; A turns a row to Keep and back, X
deletes the rows still marked Delete off the window's thread, B goes back and deletes nothing. After an install it
lists the packages RPCS3 installed without a problem (they take as much room as their game); a package kept is
noted in the app's settings (its place, size and time: library.kept_key()) and is no row of Your games, nor
installed again by X Install all, until the file changes; the licenses stay. RB Remove game on a game (owner,
30-10-2026, as shadPS4 Manager's) opens the same page: a disc game's folder in Games\PS3 and its update in
dev_hdd0\game as rows of their own, or an installed game's folder in dev_hdd0\game, and its Steam shortcut, taken out
with Steam closed for it (library.removal()). The saves and the licenses are never on the page. A game whose folder
is a game folder itself, or a disc game outside the app's folders, is never offered: the status line says to delete
it by hand.

Breaking. No folder is chosen or browsed to any more (owner, 30-10-2026): LB Folders with its added folders, usual
places and folder browser, LB Firmware with its browser and RB Packages with its browser and its Y marks are gone;
folders added before are no longer looked in (library.folders(), set_folders(), suggested() and userdata.packages()
removed, MainWindow's roots argument too). LB on Your games is Steam artwork now, RB Remove game. The Log pane shows
where Games\PS3 is.

Fixed. The newest lines of the Log pane stay at its bottom when the rows above them wrap to two lines once laid out
(a long folder): they were scrolled before the layout was done.

