Changelog: 30-10-2026 21:48:01

Release 3.0.0.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 21:19:45

Breaking. A game quits with View, LB and RB held together for two seconds, no longer View and Menu (owner,
30-10-2026): View and Menu are Windows' and Steam's guide button (Windows' "Use View + Menu as Guide button in
apps", Steam Input's Select + Start), so holding them opened the XBOX overlay or Steam's over the game, which took
the focus and left the game's own quit question unreachable. The play mode closes the emulator on the new chord
(core's play.py); the line at the bottom of Your games, the help and the wiki say so. A short press of View and Menu
still opens RPCS3's own menu, where Windows and Steam leave them to it.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 19:43:48

Release 2.1.0.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 17:55:08

Added. The battery is last in the status line at the top, at the right, and says Plugged in on the charger (owner,
30-10-2026; core's power.text()).

Changelog: 30-10-2026 17:18:10

Fixed. Steam started by the app signs in, in Desktop and in XBOX mode (core's outside_bundle(), owner, 30-10-2026): it
inherited the controller reader's SDL_VIDEODRIVER=dummy, so Steam made its login window without a window and stayed
Logged Off. X Play, the restart after Update Steam and a game started without Steam no longer get those variables.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 16:11:24

Release 2.0.0.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 14:55:47

Breaking. A game's Steam shortcut starts the app's play mode (owner, 30-10-2026: "Hold View + Menu, everywhere"):
RPCS3-Manager.exe --play --no-gui --fullscreen "<EBOOT.BIN>", which starts RPCS3 in its folder and ends with it, so
its Steam number and artwork names change. A shortcut made before, which starts rpcs3.exe itself, is still the
game's: it shows (Update Steam), and Y Update Steam writes it again (shortcuts.outdated()).

Changelog: 30-10-2026 14:55:47

Added. Hold View and Menu together for two seconds to quit a game (core's play mode): RPCS3 closes as its window
would, from Steam's library, X Play or without Steam. The line at the bottom says so when a game starts ("In the game,
hold View and Menu together to quit."), and Your games' information and the wiki chapter. A short press still opens
RPCS3's own menu with Exit Game. The app turns RPCS3's question before a game's window closes off (CurrentSettings.ini,
[main_window] confirmationBoxExitGame=false), so that close does not stop at "Exit Game?".

Changelog: 30-10-2026 13:35:58

Breaking. The Open Steam row at the top of Your games is gone (owner, 30-10-2026): Steam's library opens from the
portal, RT Steam.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 13:35:58

Added. On a device without Steam (not installed, or never started), X Play starts the game in RPCS3 itself, full
screen, with the command its Steam shortcut has (shortcuts.command(), core's platform.start_program() outside the
app's bundle; owner, 30-10-2026: a fallback, as a game cannot be played without Steam otherwise). Without RPCS3
installed it says to install it first. With Steam installed X plays through Steam as before.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 12:54:34

Fixed. Steam started by the app signs in (core, owner, 30-10-2026): X Play and the restart after Steam's shortcuts
changed started steam.exe by the lower-case name in Steam's registry key, and a Steam started so never signed in, its
login window off the screen; it is started by its name as on the disk now, outside the app's bundle. The information
popup's text box is as high as its text, up to 0.7 of the window: a text with "[PS3] <title>" in it was measured as
HTML and kept four lines high.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 01:30:27

Release 1.0.1.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 23:14:12

Fixed. Update Steam starts Steam again signed in (core's with_steam_closed(): a plain steam.exe on Windows; owner,
29-10-2026): the steam.exe -silent it started never signed in, so a game's Play and Open Steam did nothing until
Steam was started by hand. The status line says Steam was started again, signed in.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 21:56:04

Release 1.0.0.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 21:44:22

Breaking. X on a game no longer steps its screen (owner, 29-10-2026: X plays the game now): Screen (16:9, 4:3, Fill
screen) is a setting of the Settings pane's Picture tab instead, for every game, in config\config.yml (Aspect ratio
and Stretch To Display Area), in place of the Fill the screen switch, which it covers. A game's own settings that the
app wrote before stay, and RPCS3 still reads them first for that game; the list no longer shows a game's screen.

Added. X Play on a game of Your games that is in Steam starts it through Steam (steam://rungameid, Steam started
first when it does not run; owner, 29-10-2026: a game started from the manager); a game not in Steam yet says how it
gets there. Open Steam, a row at the top of Your games, opens Steam's library in Big Picture (A Open Steam). Every
browser of the app opens again in the folder last taken or picked a file in (core's browse.remembered), while it is
there. RB Packages installs several files at once (owner, 29-10-2026: not one by one): Y marks a file in the packages
browser (a ✓ before it), X then installs the marked ones only, licenses first and updates last, as the folder's; the
marks go when another folder opens.

Fixed. The Log pane's newest lines were a label that grew past the pane and was cut off at the top (owner,
29-10-2026): they are a view of their own now, its newest line in view, which a finger scrolls; a tap on it shows the
whole log as A does.

Fixed. A game whose card was taken out no longer ends Update Steam: Game.picture() answers no picture where Windows
raises for the empty card slot (WinError 1005), as shadPS4 Manager's does.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 17:05:12

Release 0.1.0.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 16:28:00

Added. The BC250 suite's RPCS3 Manager on the portable window (owner, 29-10-2026: "finish the gaming category,
starting with RPCS3"), laid out as PPSSPP Manager: four cards, RPCS3, Your games, Settings and Log, the actions with a
controller button in the row at the bottom. A Install downloads RPCS3 0.0.43-20395 for Windows, the build the BC250
suite's app pins (rpcs3-v0.0.43-20395-46b7fb67_win64_msvc.7z, 37 MB, from RPCS3/rpcs3-binaries-win), checks it
against the pinned SHA-256 and unpacks it with Windows' own tar (the .7z uses the BCJ2 filter, which no Python package
reads) into %LOCALAPPDATA%\windows-portable-suite\windows-portable-rpcs3\emulator\, where RPCS3 on Windows keeps
everything beside its program (config\, dev_hdd0\, dev_flash\, GuiConfigs\, log\); X Remove RPCS3, with a second
press, deletes only the files the archive brought; Y Update when an older build is there. The RPCS3 pane says when
Microsoft's Visual C++ runtime is missing. LB Firmware: the app's folder browser in Downloads showing the .PUP files,
and RPCS3 installs the one picked without any window (--headless --installfw; the result from its log, log\RPCS3.log,
and the version from dev_flash); RB Packages: the browser showing the .pkg files and the .rap and .edat licenses, X
installs the open folder's (the licenses first, then the packages, a game's update last) and A on a file that one,
each in a run of RPCS3 without its window (--headless --installpkg), the outcome from RPCS3's log. Before RPCS3's
first start the app turns its welcome dialog and its update check off (GuiConfigs\CurrentSettings.ini) and writes
player 1 on the device's controller through RPCS3's XInput handler with RPCS3's default layout, in which View and
Menu together (or the guide button) open RPCS3's menu with Exit Game (config\input_configs\global\Default.yml; a
file RPCS3 wrote is never touched). Your games: the disc games in the chosen folders (PS3_DISC.SFB and PS3_GAME; one
without its PS3_DISC.SFB is said so), the games installed in RPCS3's dev_hdd0 and the disc games RPCS3 knows, read as
the BC250 app reads them; played from Steam, never from the app (owner, 29-10-2026), alone and full screen (--no-gui
--fullscreen: RPCS3 ends with the game); A Steam mark and Y Update Steam put them in Steam as "[PS3] <title>" (RPCS3
and its firmware installed first), with the game's own pictures and a cover from SteamGridDB with the suite's key (RB
Steam artwork); X Screen steps the game's screen (16:9, 4:3, Fill screen) in its own settings in RPCS3; LB Folders,
with the folder browser for the controller. Settings in four tabs (Picture, Speed, Sound, Messages: 15 settings of
config\config.yml, RPCS3 0.0.43's own keys and defaults, Cubeb and XAudio2 for the sound on Windows), never written
while RPCS3 runs. The Log: RPCS3's folder with the firmware, the installed games and the saves, and the app's log; A
View log (or a tap) shows the whole log in the app. The suite's buttons (B back, View exit, Menu the information), the
d-pad staying in a pane, no pill in a pane and no user name on the screen or in the log, as in every app of the suite.
Not carried over from the BC250 app: the controller state in the header (the handheld's controller is built in), the
desktop's volume for RPCS3 (Bazzite's), RPCS3's own window for its other settings. A removable drive without a card
(an empty SD slot) is left out of the folders offered and of the browser's places (core), rather than ending the
app.

